  "name": "Chirimía y tun (Guatemalan highland Maya shawm and drum)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Shawm-and-drum music of the K'iche' and other highland Maya of Guatemala, played for cofradía processions, saints' feasts and masked dance-dramas, notably at Chichicastenango. The chirimía, a double-reed shawm brought in the colonial period, plays long modal melodies over a large drum and the tun slit drum. The dulzaina card stands in for the chirimía and the maguaré card for the tun.",
